/* ---------- Science (bilingual pairs) ---------- */
const SCIENCE = [
  { zh: "光在真空中每秒行进约 299,792 公里。你此刻看到的阳光，是 8 分 20 秒前从太阳出发的。", en: "Light travels at about 299,792 kilometres per second in a vacuum. The sunlight you see now left the Sun 8 minutes and 20 seconds ago." },
  { zh: "月光到达地球只需约 1.3 秒。所以你看到的月亮，是 1.3 秒前的月亮。", en: "Moonlight takes only about 1.3 seconds to reach Earth, so the Moon you see is the Moon of 1.3 seconds ago." },
  { zh: "人体由大约 37 万亿个细胞组成，而住在你身体里和体表的微生物约有 38 万亿个，和你的细胞数大致相当。", en: "Your body is made of roughly 37 trillion cells, and the microbes living in and on you number about 38 trillion, about the same order of magnitude." },
  { zh: "一个细胞里的 DNA 展开约有 2 米长。把全身的 DNA 首尾相连，长度相当于地球到太阳往返数十次。", en: "The DNA in a single cell stretches about 2 metres. Joined end to end, all your DNA would reach to the Sun and back dozens of times." },
  { zh: "人的心脏一生大约跳动 25 亿次，从不停工，也没有备件。", en: "A human heart beats about 2.5 billion times in a lifetime, without a pause and without spare parts." },
  { zh: "大脑运行只需约 20 瓦功率，和一只昏暗的灯泡差不多，却运行着你的全部思维、记忆和情绪。", en: "The brain runs on about 20 watts, roughly a dim light bulb, yet it powers all your thoughts, memories and feelings." },
  { zh: "最快的神经信号在身体里以约每秒 120 米的速度传递，慢的只有每秒 1 米左右。所以踩到尖东西时，痛感总是迟到一点点。", en: "The fastest nerve signals travel at about 120 metres per second; the slowest manage barely 1 metre per second. That is why pain from a stubbed toe arrives a fraction late." },
  { zh: "成年人有 206 块骨头，婴儿出生时却有约 300 块，其中许多会在成长中融合成一块。", en: "Adults have 206 bones, but babies are born with around 300; many fuse together as they grow." },
  { zh: "皮肤是人体最大的器官，成年人的皮肤总面积约 2 平方米，重约 3.6 公斤。", en: "Skin is the body's largest organ: an adult's skin covers about 2 square metres and weighs roughly 3.6 kilograms." },
  { zh: "一个红细胞在身体里跑完一整圈循环，平均只需要大约一分钟。", en: "A red blood cell takes only about a minute, on average, to complete a full circuit of your body." },
  { zh: "人每天眨眼约 15,000 到 20,000 次。加起来，相当于每天有近半小时，你是闭着眼度过的。", en: "You blink roughly 15,000 to 20,000 times a day, which adds up to nearly half an hour spent with your eyes shut." },
  { zh: "早上刚起床时，你比晚上高约 1 到 2 厘米：脊柱的椎间盘白天被体重压扁，夜里平躺后又慢慢恢复。", en: "You are about 1 to 2 centimetres taller in the morning than at night: the discs in your spine compress by day and recover as you lie flat." },
  { zh: "蜂鸟每秒可以扇动翅膀约 80 次，心跳每分钟可以超过 1,200 次，是哺乳动物里代谢最疯狂的引擎之一。", en: "A hummingbird can beat its wings about 80 times per second, and its heart can race at over 1,200 beats per minute." },
  { zh: "章鱼有三颗心脏，血液是蓝色的，因为它用含铜的血蓝蛋白而不是含铁的血红蛋白来运送氧气。", en: "Octopuses have three hearts and blue blood, because they carry oxygen with copper-based haemocyanin instead of iron-based haemoglobin." },
  { zh: "野生长颈鹿每天的睡眠常常不足 2 小时，而且大多是站着打的几分钟小盹。", en: "Wild giraffes often sleep less than two hours a day, mostly in short naps taken standing up." },
  { zh: "大象能用脚感知地面传来的低频震动，隔着几公里和同伴“说话”。它们的脚，某种意义上是耳朵。", en: "Elephants can feel low-frequency rumbles through the ground with their feet, 'talking' to each other across kilometres. Their feet are, in a sense, ears." },
  { zh: "一只蜜蜂忙碌一生，大约只能酿出十二分之一茶匙的蜂蜜。一罐蜂蜜背后，是成千上万只蜜蜂的一生。", en: "A single bee produces only about one-twelfth of a teaspoon of honey in its whole life. Behind one jar stand thousands of lifetimes." },
  { zh: "鲨鱼在地球上已经存在了约 4.5 亿年，比最早的树木还要早几千万年。树长出来之前，鲨鱼已经游了很久了。", en: "Sharks have existed for about 450 million years, tens of millions of years before the first trees. Sharks were already ancient when forests began." },
  { zh: "真菌与动物的亲缘关系，比与植物更近。你和一朵蘑菇的共同祖先，比蘑菇和一棵树的共同祖先更晚近。", en: "Fungi are more closely related to animals than to plants. You share a more recent common ancestor with a mushroom than a mushroom shares with a tree." },
  { zh: "人类约有 60% 的基因，能在香蕉里找到对应版本。生命用的是同一套零件库，只是组装方式不同。", en: "About 60 percent of human genes have a recognisable counterpart in a banana. Life uses one shared parts catalogue, assembled differently." },
  { zh: "从植物学上说，草莓并不是真正的浆果，香蕉反而是。分类学经常和日常语言唱反调。", en: "Botanically, a strawberry is not a true berry, but a banana is. Taxonomy often disagrees with everyday language." },
  { zh: "马里亚纳海沟的挑战者深渊深约 10,900 米，比珠穆朗玛峰的高度还要深。把珠峰沉进去，峰顶离海面还差 2 公里多。", en: "The Challenger Deep in the Mariana Trench lies about 10,900 metres down, deeper than Everest is tall. Drop Everest in and its peak would still be 2 kilometres underwater." },
  { zh: "在赤道上，地球自转的线速度约每小时 1,670 公里。你坐着不动，其实一直在以这个速度向东飞驰。", en: "At the equator, Earth's spin carries you eastward at about 1,670 kilometres per hour. Sitting still, you are still flying." },
  { zh: "地球绕太阳公转的速度约为每秒 30 公里。读完这句话的几秒钟里，你已经在太空里移动了上百公里。", en: "Earth orbits the Sun at about 30 kilometres per second. In the few seconds it took to read this, you travelled hundreds of kilometres through space." },
  { zh: "太阳大得可以装下大约 130 万个地球。", en: "About 1.3 million Earths would fit inside the Sun." },
  { zh: "一茶匙中子星物质重约数十亿吨。中子星是恒星死亡后被引力压到极致的残骸。", en: "A teaspoon of neutron star would weigh roughly a billion tonnes. A neutron star is a dead star crushed by gravity to the very limit." },
  { zh: "银河系中心藏着一个名为人马座 A* 的黑洞，质量约是太阳的 400 万倍。我们整个太阳系，正绕着它缓慢旋转。", en: "At the centre of the Milky Way sits Sagittarius A*, a black hole about 4 million times the mass of the Sun. Our whole solar system slowly orbits it." },
  { zh: "可观测宇宙中估计至少有约 2,000 亿个星系，每个星系里又有成百上千亿颗恒星。", en: "The observable universe holds an estimated 200 billion galaxies at least, each with hundreds of billions of stars." },
  { zh: "宇宙的年龄约为 138 亿年。你身体里的大部分氢原子，就是在那最初的时刻形成的。", en: "The universe is about 13.8 billion years old. Most of the hydrogen atoms in your body were forged in its very first moments." },
  { zh: "闪电的温度可达约 30,000 开尔文，大约是太阳表面温度的 5 倍。一瞬间，空气被加热到爆炸般膨胀，那就是雷声。", en: "Lightning can reach about 30,000 kelvin, roughly five times hotter than the Sun's surface. The explosive expansion of that heated air is thunder." },
  { zh: "水在 4 摄氏度时密度最大。所以湖水从表面开始结冰，冰浮在上面像一床被子，让水下的生命熬过冬天。", en: "Water is densest at 4 degrees Celsius, so lakes freeze from the top down. The floating ice acts as a blanket, letting life below survive the winter." },
  { zh: "老教堂玻璃窗下厚上薄，并不是因为玻璃像液体一样流了几百年，而是当年吹制玻璃的工艺本身就不均匀。", en: "Old church windows are thicker at the bottom not because glass flows like a liquid over centuries, but because early glassmaking was uneven." },
  { zh: "钻石和铅笔芯都是纯碳。同样是碳原子，排列成四面体就是钻石，排列成层片就是石墨。结构即命运。", en: "Diamonds and pencil lead are both pure carbon. Arranged in tetrahedra, carbon becomes diamond; arranged in sheets, graphite. Structure is destiny." },
  { zh: "人体会发出微弱的可见光，是新陈代谢的副产品，只是强度比肉眼能察觉的极限弱约 1,000 倍。你在发光，只是没人看得见。", en: "The human body glows faintly in visible light, a by-product of metabolism, but about 1,000 times dimmer than the eye can detect. You are shining; no one can see it." },
  { zh: "即使是同卵双胞胎，指纹也不相同。指纹在子宫里形成时，还受到羊水流动等微小随机因素的影响。", en: "Even identical twins have different fingerprints. They form in the womb under tiny random influences, such as the flow of amniotic fluid." },
  { zh: "任意两个人的 DNA 约有 99.9% 相同。人与人之间全部的差异，只写在那 0.1% 里。", en: "Any two humans share about 99.9 percent of their DNA. Every difference between us is written in the remaining 0.1 percent." },
  { zh: "人类与黑猩猩的 DNA 相似度约为 98.8%。分家的时间，大约在 600 万年前。", en: "Humans and chimpanzees share about 98.8 percent of their DNA. The two lineages parted roughly 6 million years ago." },
  { zh: "你细胞里的线粒体，来自约 20 亿年前被远古细胞吞下的一种细菌。它只通过母亲传给你。", en: "Your mitochondria descend from bacteria swallowed by an ancient cell about 2 billion years ago, and you inherit them only from your mother." },
  { zh: "已知最古老的一棵单体树，是一棵狐尾松，年龄约 5,000 岁。它发芽的时候，金字塔还没建完。", en: "The oldest known individual tree, a bristlecone pine, is about 5,000 years old. It sprouted before the pyramids were finished." },
  { zh: "蓝鲸的心脏重约 180 公斤，主动脉粗到可以让一个小孩爬过去。", en: "A blue whale's heart weighs about 180 kilograms, and its aorta is wide enough for a small child to crawl through." },
  { zh: "考拉的指纹与人类极其相似，在显微镜下都难以分辨，甚至可能干扰犯罪现场的指纹鉴定。", en: "Koala fingerprints are so similar to human ones that they are hard to tell apart under a microscope, and could in principle contaminate a crime scene." },
  { zh: "在海马的世界里，怀孕生子的是雄性。雌海马把卵放进雄性的育儿袋，接下来的一切由父亲完成。", en: "Among seahorses, it is the male who becomes pregnant. The female places her eggs in his brood pouch, and he does the rest." },
  { zh: "灯塔水母在受伤或衰老时，可以把自己的细胞退回幼体状态重新来过，因此被称作“不死水母”。", en: "The jellyfish Turritopsis dohrnii can revert its cells to a juvenile stage when injured or old, earning it the name 'immortal jellyfish'." },
  { zh: "蚂蚁能搬动约自身体重 50 倍的重物。按比例放大到人类，相当于一个人举起一辆小汽车。", en: "An ant can carry about 50 times its own body weight. Scaled to human size, that would be like lifting a small car." },
  { zh: "北极熊的毛并不是白色的，每根毛都是透明中空的，看起来白，是因为光线在其中反复散射。", en: "Polar bear fur is not white. Each hair is a translucent hollow tube; it looks white because of how light scatters inside it." },
  { zh: "变色龙变色不是靠换颜料，而是调节皮肤里纳米晶体的间距，改变反射光的颜色。", en: "Chameleons change colour not by swapping pigments but by adjusting the spacing of nanocrystals in their skin, changing the light they reflect." },
  { zh: "猫头鹰的眼球是管状的，无法在眼窝里转动。作为补偿，它的脖子能转约 270 度。", en: "An owl's eyes are tube-shaped and cannot move in their sockets. To compensate, its neck can rotate about 270 degrees." },
  { zh: "金鱼的记忆可以保持数月甚至更久，“金鱼只有 7 秒记忆”是个流传很广的谣言。", en: "A goldfish's memory lasts for months. The famous 'seven-second memory' is a myth." },
  { zh: "睡眠时，大脑的类淋巴系统会加速清除白天积累的代谢废物。熬夜，等于跳过一次大脑的夜间保洁。", en: "During sleep, the brain's glymphatic system speeds up clearing the day's metabolic waste. Skipping sleep means skipping the night cleaning crew." },
  { zh: "据估计，人一生大约有 6 年时间在做梦。只是绝大多数梦，在醒来几分钟内就被忘了。", en: "By some estimates, we spend roughly six years of our lives dreaming, though most dreams are forgotten within minutes of waking." },
  { zh: "并不存在“左脑型”或“右脑型”的人。脑成像显示，两个半球始终在协同工作。", en: "There is no such thing as a 'left-brained' or 'right-brained' person. Brain imaging shows both hemispheres working together all the time." },
  { zh: "“我们只用了 10% 的大脑”是个谣言。一天之内，成像技术能在几乎所有脑区都观测到活动。", en: "The idea that we use only 10 percent of our brains is a myth. Over the course of a day, imaging detects activity in virtually every region." },
  { zh: "舌头上的“味觉地图”是谣言：舌头的每个区域都能尝到甜、酸、咸、苦和鲜，只是敏感度略有差别。", en: "The tongue map is a myth: every region of the tongue can taste sweet, sour, salty, bitter and umami, with only slight differences in sensitivity." },
  { zh: "拿破仑并不矮。他的身高约 168 厘米，在当时的法国属于平均水平。“小个子”印象来自英制与法制单位的混淆和英国漫画的抹黑。", en: "Napoleon was not short: at about 168 centimetres he was average for a Frenchman of his time. The 'little corporal' myth came from confused units and British caricatures." },
  { zh: "胡夫金字塔建成时，地球上还有猛犸象活着。最后一批猛犸象在弗兰格尔岛上活到了约公元前 1700 年。", en: "When the Great Pyramid of Giza was built, mammoths still walked the Earth. The last of them survived on Wrangel Island until about 1700 BC." },
  { zh: "克利奥帕特拉生活的年代，离今天约 2,000 年，离金字塔建成约 2,500 年。也就是说，她离 iPhone 比离金字塔更近。", en: "Cleopatra lived about 2,000 years before us, but some 2,500 years after the pyramids were built. She lived closer in time to the iPhone than to the Great Pyramid." },
  { zh: "牛津大学比阿兹特克帝国还要古老：牛津在 1096 年就已开始授课，而阿兹特克的首都特诺奇蒂特兰建于 1325 年。", en: "Oxford University is older than the Aztec Empire: teaching at Oxford began in 1096, while the Aztec capital Tenochtitlan was founded in 1325." },
  { zh: "任天堂创立于 1889 年，那时中国还处在清朝光绪年间。它最早是卖手工绘制的花札纸牌的。", en: "Nintendo was founded in 1889, during China's Qing dynasty. It began by selling hand-painted hanafuda playing cards." },
  { zh: "土星的平均密度约 0.69 克每立方厘米，比水还小。如果有一个足够大的海洋，土星会浮在水面上。", en: "Saturn's average density is about 0.69 grams per cubic centimetre, less than water. In a large enough ocean, Saturn would float." },
  { zh: "金星上的一天比一年还长：它自转一周约需 243 个地球日，绕太阳公转一周却只需约 225 个地球日。", en: "A single day on Venus, one full rotation, takes about 243 Earth days, while its year takes only about 225. On Venus, a day outlasts a year." },
  { zh: "在火星上，日落是蓝色的。火星稀薄的大气散射光线的方式，恰好和地球相反。", en: "On Mars, sunsets glow blue. Its thin atmosphere scatters light in almost the opposite way to Earth's." },
  { zh: "木星的大红斑是一场比地球还宽的风暴，已经刮了至少几百年。", en: "Jupiter's Great Red Spot is a storm wider than the entire Earth, and it has been raging for centuries." },
  { zh: "月球正在以每年约 3.8 厘米的速度远离地球。阿波罗宇航员留在月面上的激光反射镜，至今还在帮我们量这个距离。", en: "The Moon is drifting away from Earth at about 3.8 centimetres per year, measured with laser reflectors the Apollo astronauts left on its surface." },
  { zh: "地球不是一个完美的球：赤道半径比极半径大约 21 公里，因为自转把它“甩”得微微鼓起。", en: "Earth is not a perfect sphere. Its equatorial radius is about 21 kilometres larger than its polar radius, because its spin makes it bulge." },
  { zh: "地核的温度约为 6,000 摄氏度，几乎和太阳表面一样热。你脚下几千公里深处，藏着一个太阳表面。", en: "Earth's core is about 6,000 degrees Celsius, roughly as hot as the surface of the Sun. A piece of the Sun's surface sits thousands of kilometres beneath your feet." },
  { zh: "海水中溶解着约 2,000 万吨黄金，只是浓度太低，捞出来的成本远比金子本身贵。", en: "The oceans hold about 20 million tonnes of dissolved gold, but it is so dilute that recovering it would cost far more than the gold is worth." },
  { zh: "南极冰盖储存了地球上约六成的淡水。如果它全部融化，全球海平面将上升约 58 米。", en: "Antarctica's ice sheet stores roughly 60 percent of the world's fresh water. If it all melted, sea levels would rise by about 58 metres." },
  { zh: "珠穆朗玛峰每年大约长高 4 毫米，因为印度板块还在持续挤压欧亚板块。世界最高峰，仍在长个子。", en: "Mount Everest grows about 4 millimetres taller each year, as the Indian plate keeps pushing into the Eurasian plate." },
  { zh: "死海的盐度约 34%，接近普通海水的 10 倍。在那里游泳，人会不由自主地浮在水面上。", en: "The Dead Sea is about 34 percent salt, nearly ten times saltier than the ocean. Swimmers there float whether they want to or not." },
];

